From d5cbd08d702e4eebae791d07c0d9740348929d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:41:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/49] strict-load-checks: fail loudly on

The essential-ROM check originally guarded only the CoCo 3's Super ECB;
every other machine still booted silently against a missing or wrong
BASIC ROM, executing garbage from the reset vector while the run looked
healthy.  Extend the same policy to the Dragon family and the MC-10,
keyed on the CRC verdict each machine's existing rombank_verify_crc call
already produces -- no new CRC lists.  Only the image the machine cannot
reach a BASIC prompt without is required: a 4K CoCo's Extended BASIC,
the Dragon 64's 64K-mode ROM and the Dragon Professional's BOOT (whose
verify upstream deliberately discards) all stay optional.  The Dragon
family shares one dragon_require_rom() helper; the MC-10's check is
inline, same as the CoCo 3's.
